00:26:53.840 --> 00:26:54.640
And name and address.
姓名和地址。

644
00:26:54.640 --> 00:26:57.980
Yeah, it was like an alphabetical list of everyone in your city.
是啊，那就像是一份你所在城市所有人的字母顺序名单。

645
00:26:58.920 --> 00:27:03.400
And I remember getting it as a kid and like looking us up and being like, there we are.
我记得小时候收到它时，会去查我们家，然后说，看，我们在那儿。

646
00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:07.460
Ours always had like a little star or circle by someone we knew.
我们家的那本上面总会有个小星星或者圆圈，标记着我们认识的人。

647
00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:10.120
Like my mom would have gone through and like made little markings.
就像我妈妈会翻阅它，然后做些小记号。

648
00:27:10.360 --> 00:27:10.680
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

649
00:27:10.760 --> 00:27:11.720
Or you earmark it.
或者你会折角做标记。

650
00:27:11.800 --> 00:27:12.000
Yeah.
是啊。

651
00:27:12.360 --> 00:27:17.840
Well, the yellow pages was a directory of all of the businesses in your area.
嗯，黄页是你们当地所有企业的名录。

652
00:27:17.980 --> 00:27:21.760
And they were listed alphabetically by the type of business.
它们是按企业类型以字母顺序排列的。

653
00:27:21.760 --> 00:27:22.400
Right.
没错。

654
00:27:22.500 --> 00:27:23.380
Like floriSt.
比如花店。

655
00:27:23.600 --> 00:27:24.100
Yes.
是的。

656
00:27:24.240 --> 00:27:27.440
If you needed an electrician, you looked in the electrician section.
如果你需要电工，就去查电工那一栏。

657
00:27:27.940 --> 00:27:33.540
And different businesses might take out ads so that their listing was bigger or flashier,
不同的商家可能会投放广告，让他们的条目看起来更大、更显眼，

658
00:27:33.660 --> 00:27:34.620
like a half page.
比如半个版面那么大。

659
00:27:34.980 --> 00:27:35.200
Yeah.
是啊。

660
00:27:35.200 --> 00:27:42.320
And that's why a lot of businesses would put the letter A somewhere in the name, like awesome plumbers.
所以很多商家会在名字里加个字母A，比如“一流管道工”。

661
00:27:42.440 --> 00:27:42.640
Yes.
没错。

662
00:27:42.740 --> 00:27:45.400
Because then they would be at the top of the liSt.
因为这样他们就能排在列表的最前面。

663
00:27:45.700 --> 00:27:46.180
Yes.
是的。

664
00:27:46.380 --> 00:27:51.440
And then there were also the blue pages, which is a government directory.
此外还有蓝页，那是政府部门的名录。

665
00:27:51.560 --> 00:27:53.060
I never got a blue page.
我从来没见过蓝页。

666
00:27:53.060 --> 00:27:54.440
I've never heard of the blue pages.
我都没听说过蓝页。

667
00:27:54.580 --> 00:27:55.900
Well, they could be at your library.
嗯，你们图书馆里可能就有。

668
00:27:56.140 --> 00:27:56.320
Oh.
噢。

669
00:27:56.320 --> 00:28:00.580
You could look in the blue pages if you needed to contact a government agency in your area.
如果你需要联系当地的政府机构，就可以查蓝页。

670
00:28:00.600 --> 00:28:02.220
Like the water department for your city.
比如你们市的水务局。

671
00:28:02.400 --> 00:28:02.780
Yes.
没错。

672
00:28:03.160 --> 00:28:06.280
But when I saw the yellow pages, I got really nostalgic.
但当我看到黄页时，我真的感到很怀旧。

673
00:28:06.280 --> 00:28:11.680
And I was like, as a kid, I would flip through the yellow pages and look at the ads.
我就想，小时候我经常翻看黄页，看上面的广告。

674
00:28:11.900 --> 00:28:17.020
Like, I would read the comics in the newspaper that we got every day at our house.
就像我每天在家里看报纸上的连环画一样。

675
00:28:17.140 --> 00:28:17.820
Yeah, the funnies.
对，就是滑稽漫画。

676
00:28:17.820 --> 00:28:18.700
The funnies.
滑稽漫画。

677
00:28:19.060 --> 00:28:26.000
And like, I would read the back of the cereal box at breakfast because we didn't have smartphones or internet.
还有吃早餐时读麦片盒的背面，因为那时我们没有智能手机或互联网。

678
00:28:26.280 --> 00:28:26.600
Right.
没错。

679
00:28:26.780 --> 00:28:29.740
I would flip through the Sears catalog, circling stuff.
我会翻看西尔斯百货的商品目录，把想要的东西圈出来。

680
00:28:30.040 --> 00:28:32.240
Oh, how great was it to get a catalog?
噢，收到商品目录多棒啊？

681
00:28:32.620 --> 00:28:33.880
I love a catalog.
我喜欢商品目录。

682
00:28:34.080 --> 00:28:34.920
I still love a catalog.
我现在依然喜欢。

683
00:28:34.920 --> 00:28:36.040
I do still love a catalog.
我确实还是很喜欢。

684
00:28:36.900 --> 00:28:39.520
Anyway, well, there you go for you youngins.
总之，年轻人，这就是你们错过的乐趣。

685
00:28:39.720 --> 00:28:41.660
All the fun you missed out on.
你们错过了所有这些好玩的事。

686
00:28:41.800 --> 00:28:45.920
Anytime you want a breakdown of some old tech, just hit up these two middle-aged ladies.
任何时候想了解旧科技，尽管来问我们这两位中年女士。

687
00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:46.580
We'll tell you.
我们会告诉你们的。

688
00:28:48.020 --> 00:28:50.500
Oh, now we have Pam's storyline.
噢，现在轮到帕姆的故事线了。

689
00:28:51.060 --> 00:28:51.540
Yes.
没错。

690
00:28:51.740 --> 00:28:54.180
She's on the hunt for the RSVPs.
她在收集回复函。

691
00:28:54.500 --> 00:28:55.740
She starts with Kelly.
她先找了凯莉。

692
00:28:56.200 --> 00:28:59.080
Kelly wants to know if Ryan is going to the wedding.
凯莉想知道瑞安会不会去参加婚礼。

693
00:28:59.420 --> 00:29:02.420
She doesn't want to RSVP unless Ryan is going.
如果瑞安不去，她就不想回复。

694
00:29:02.740 --> 00:29:04.180
Because it would be a waste of time.
因为那样会浪费时间。

695
00:29:04.480 --> 00:29:05.880
I mean, wait, that came out wrong.
我是说，等等，这话听起来不对。

696
00:29:06.180 --> 00:29:06.620
Right.
没错。

697
00:29:06.700 --> 00:29:14.200
I mean, what she's trying to say is that she would really like it if Ryan went because then she would go and she'd really like to be there to support Jim.
我的意思是，她想表达的是，如果瑞安去的话她会很高兴，因为那样她也会去，而且她真的很想去支持吉姆。

698
00:29:15.460 --> 00:29:19.740
Everything she said to you was like, it's a frenemy moment.
她对你说的每一句话，简直就是“亦敌亦友”的时刻。

699
00:29:19.740 --> 00:29:22.560
We had a fan question from Heather B.
我们收到一个来自希瑟·B的粉丝提问，

700
00:29:22.780 --> 00:29:24.360
in Victoria, British Columbia.
她来自不列颠哥伦比亚省的维多利亚市。

701
00:29:24.960 --> 00:29:32.560
At 5 minutes, 48 seconds, when Pam goes to Kelly's desk, there is a sign that says Kelly's Nook.
在5分48秒时，帕姆走到凯莉的办公桌前，那里有个写着“凯莉的小角落”的牌子。

702
00:29:32.860 --> 00:29:33.300
Oh!
噢！

703
00:29:33.660 --> 00:29:34.460
And there is.
确实有。

704
00:29:34.640 --> 00:29:39.480
And, you know, before she had her little nameplate that said Kelly that she got in the Yankee swap.
而且，你知道，在那之前她有个小名牌，写着“凯莉”，是她在洋基交换礼物活动上得到的。

705
00:29:39.720 --> 00:29:41.160
But this is a new sign.
但这块牌子是新的。

706
00:29:41.360 --> 00:29:42.900
It says Kelly's Nook.
上面写着“凯莉的小角落”。

707
00:29:42.900 --> 00:29:44.200
I love a Nook.
我喜欢“小角落”这个词。

708
00:29:44.580 --> 00:29:45.400
Heather B.
希瑟·B。

709
00:29:45.980 --> 00:29:51.960
wondered if this was an addition from the scene when she told Dwight to get out of her Nook.
想知道这是否是她叫德怀特离开她的小角落那场戏之后加的。

710
00:29:55.000 --> 00:29:57.680
Well, this scene is going to take us to a Pam talking head.
嗯，这场戏将把我们带到帕姆的访谈片段。

711
00:29:58.120 --> 00:30:00.800
And Pam and Jim have clearly done that thing.
帕姆和吉姆显然已经做了那件事。

712
00:30:00.900 --> 00:30:02.760
The destination wedding, you guys.
目的地婚礼，伙计们。

713
00:30:02.920 --> 00:30:06.760
If your friend has a destination wedding, it's because they're trying to rule out some people.
如果你的朋友举办目的地婚礼，那是因为他们想排除掉一些人。

714
00:30:06.940 --> 00:30:08.180
I think that's true.
我觉得确实如此。

715
00:30:08.180 --> 00:30:12.560
Because you're allowed to have a smaller guest list if it's a destination wedding.
因为如果是目的地婚礼，你就可以缩减宾客名单。

716
00:30:12.760 --> 00:30:13.180
That's right.
没错。

717
00:30:13.180 --> 00:30:18.600
You don't expect everyone to go with you to, like, a remote area or, like, a fancy vacation.
你不会指望每个人都跟你去什么偏远地区或者高档度假胜地。

718
00:30:18.600 --> 00:30:20.200
I'm getting married on a boat.
我要在船上结婚。

719
00:30:20.560 --> 00:30:20.920
What?
什么？

720
00:30:21.340 --> 00:30:25.720
Well, it is revealed that Jim and Pam are getting married in Niagara Falls.
嗯，剧情揭示了吉姆和帕姆要在尼亚加拉大瀑布结婚。

721
00:30:25.960 --> 00:30:26.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

722
00:30:26.540 --> 00:30:31.220
Now, when we traded emails with Warren and Halstead about their episode, Cafe Disco,
现在，当我们和沃伦还有霍尔斯特德通过邮件交流关于他们那集《咖啡迪斯科》时，

723
00:30:31.900 --> 00:30:35.660
Halstead reminded me that in an earlier version of the script,
霍尔斯特德提醒我，在剧本的早期版本中，

724
00:30:35.900 --> 00:30:37.980
Pam and Jim were going to get married in Paris.
帕姆和吉姆本打算在巴黎结婚。

725
00:30:38.540 --> 00:30:39.720
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

726
00:30:39.720 --> 00:30:40.900
I forgot that.
我把这事忘了。

727
00:30:41.280 --> 00:30:41.840
Isn't that crazy?
这不疯狂吗？

728
00:30:42.060 --> 00:30:46.040
And they changed it to Niagara because they felt like Paris, number one,
他们把地点改成了尼亚加拉，因为他们觉得巴黎，第一，

729
00:30:46.120 --> 00:30:49.700
they thought it was a little bit too kind of on-the-nose romantic,
他们觉得那有点太过于浪漫了，

730
00:30:50.600 --> 00:30:55.580
maybe too much of a stretch budget-wise, and they thought Niagara Falls was perfect.
预算上可能也太吃力了，而且他们认为尼亚加拉大瀑布非常完美。

731
00:30:56.060 --> 00:30:56.940
I agree.
我同意。

732
00:30:56.940 --> 00:31:02.300
I think that Paris just seems a little too big and too far away for who Jim and Pam are.
我觉得对于吉姆和帕姆的人设来说，巴黎显得有点太隆重、太遥远了。

733
00:31:02.460 --> 00:31:02.860
I agree.
我同意。

734
00:31:02.860 --> 00:31:08.720
Now, also speaking of Niagara Falls, we are not that far from these wedding episodes,
说到尼亚加拉大瀑布，我们离那几集婚礼戏份也不远了，

735
00:31:08.720 --> 00:31:15.660
and Randy shared with us that they were already heavily prepping that episode.
兰迪和我们分享说，他们当时已经在为那一集做大量的准备工作了。

736
00:31:15.660 --> 00:31:18.000
Like, heavily.
真的是大量的准备。

737
00:31:18.320 --> 00:31:19.700
It's a big episode.
那是一集大制作。

738
00:31:19.700 --> 00:31:21.620
We'll get there, but it's a big one.
我们会讲到那里的，但那确实很重要。

739
00:31:22.100 --> 00:31:27.220
At 6 minutes 32 seconds, we got a fan question from Emily B.
在6分32秒，我们收到了来自阿拉巴马州艾米丽·B的粉丝提问，

740
00:31:27.680 --> 00:31:29.840
in Alabama who said,
她问道：

741
00:31:29.840 --> 00:31:33.740
Behind Pam on the file cabinet by Kelly's desk,
在凯莉办公桌旁的文件柜上，帕姆身后，

742
00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:39.740
there is a Greater Scranton Chamber of Commerce business card from someone named Mary.
有一张写着玛丽名字的大斯克兰顿商会的名片。

743
00:31:40.360 --> 00:31:44.480
I looked up the current board of directors, and apparently this person is no longer active,
我查了现任董事会成员，显然这个人已经不在职了，

744
00:31:44.480 --> 00:31:48.660
but I'm curious to know why were they represented on the show.
但我很好奇为什么她会出现在剧中。

745
00:31:49.640 --> 00:31:55.720
Emily B., Mary, at the Chamber of Commerce, was like a huge help to our show.
艾米丽·B，商会的玛丽对我们的节目帮助非常大。

746
00:31:55.980 --> 00:31:57.720
Yes, she's an unsung hero.
是的，她是位无名英雄。

747
00:31:57.900 --> 00:31:59.860
Carrie Bennett shared all about her with us.
嘉莉·贝内特和我们分享了关于她的一切。

748
00:31:59.960 --> 00:32:00.300
Yeah.
是的。

749
00:32:00.300 --> 00:32:04.480
If you remember in Carrie Bennett's interview, it was from a Revisited episode,
如果你还记得嘉莉·贝内特的采访，那是来自重温系列的一集，

750
00:32:05.240 --> 00:32:07.900
Carrie shared that she created a relationship with Mary,
嘉莉分享说她和玛丽建立了联系，

751
00:32:07.900 --> 00:32:12.340
and Mary would help us get local treasures for the show.
玛丽会帮我们为节目找来当地的宝贝。

752
00:32:12.780 --> 00:32:15.180
Props, signs, pizza boxes.
道具、招牌、披萨盒。

753
00:32:15.720 --> 00:32:17.540
That is a great interview, by the way.
顺便说一句，那是一次很棒的采访。

754
00:32:17.680 --> 00:32:20.220
If you guys haven't listened to it, our interview with Carrie Bennett,
如果你们还没听过我们采访凯莉·贝内特的节目，

755
00:32:20.420 --> 00:32:23.500
who was the wardrobe designer for The Office for the first four seasons,
她曾担任《办公室》前四季的服装设计师，

756
00:32:24.040 --> 00:32:27.740
and she really was groundbreaking in what she brought to the show,
她在为节目带来的贡献上确实具有开创性，

757
00:32:27.740 --> 00:32:30.360
and the relationship with Mary was one of those things.
而她与玛丽的关系就是其中之一。

758
00:32:30.540 --> 00:32:33.280
But we put that business card in a nice prominent spot.
但我们把那张名片放在了一个显眼的好位置。

759
00:32:33.500 --> 00:32:35.520
That was our way of putting Mary on the show.
那是我们让玛丽出现在节目中的方式。

760
00:32:35.640 --> 00:32:36.280
Yay, Mary!
耶，玛丽！

761
00:32:36.280 --> 00:32:39.520
So now we get to one of my favorite scenes.
现在我们来到了我最喜欢的场景之一。

762
00:32:40.060 --> 00:32:45.200
It's Michael sitting on Andy's desk while he's trying to spy on Jim and David's meeting in the conference room,
迈克尔坐在安迪的桌子上，而安迪正试图窥探吉姆和大卫在会议室里的谈话，

763
00:32:45.200 --> 00:32:48.260
and he's just, like, throwing out random questions.
他就在那儿随口抛出各种随机的问题。

764
00:32:48.440 --> 00:32:50.720
Oh, lady, I have so much for this.
噢，女士，我为这一段准备了好多内容。

765
00:32:50.940 --> 00:32:51.820
Are you ready?
你准备好了吗？

766
00:32:52.020 --> 00:32:52.480
Yes.
准备好了。

767
00:32:52.760 --> 00:32:53.880
I love this scene.
我喜欢这个场景。

768
00:32:53.940 --> 00:32:54.760
I know you loved it.
我知道你很喜欢。

769
00:32:54.920 --> 00:32:57.700
In the episode, it starts with these two lines.
在剧集中，它是从这两句台词开始的。

770
00:32:58.020 --> 00:32:58.900
Andy says,
安迪说，

771
00:32:59.100 --> 00:33:00.380
What can I do for you, Haas?
我能为你做点什么吗，哈斯？

772
00:33:00.680 --> 00:33:03.300
Michael, staring into the conference room, says,
迈克尔盯着会议室，说道，

773
00:33:03.620 --> 00:33:04.720
How are yourselves doing?
你们自己过得怎么样？

774
00:33:04.720 --> 00:33:06.860
But Jenna, the scene was so much bigger,
但是珍娜，这个场景原本要大得多，

775
00:33:06.900 --> 00:33:09.680
and big chunks of it were edited out for time,
而且为了节省时间，很大一部分被剪掉了，

776
00:33:09.740 --> 00:33:11.920
and I feel like we need to hear the full scene.
我觉得我们需要听听完整的场景。

777
00:33:12.160 --> 00:33:15.300
I cannot believe there was more to one of my favorite scenes,
我简直不敢相信我最喜欢的场景之一竟然还有更多内容，

778
00:33:15.420 --> 00:33:16.100
and I cannot wait.
我等不及了。

779
00:33:16.340 --> 00:33:17.120
So much more.
多得多了。

780
00:33:17.360 --> 00:33:17.760
All right.
好的。

781
00:33:18.160 --> 00:33:20.060
So Andy and Michael have this exchange,
所以安迪和迈克尔有这样一段对话，

782
00:33:20.300 --> 00:33:22.580
and then, right after that,
然后，紧接着，

783
00:33:22.880 --> 00:33:23.760
this would have happened.
原本会发生这些。

784
00:33:23.760 --> 00:33:25.980
Are my sales done?
我的销售额完成了吗？

785
00:33:27.780 --> 00:33:28.960
They're good.
还不错。

786
00:33:30.200 --> 00:33:31.380
Super solid.
非常稳。

787
00:33:31.400 --> 00:33:31.840
What do you mean?
你什么意思？

788
00:33:33.120 --> 00:33:36.340
Um, your retention.
嗯，你的客户留存率。

789
00:33:36.600 --> 00:33:37.560
How that?
怎么说？

790
00:33:37.880 --> 00:33:39.200
How's your retention been?
你的留存率怎么样了？

791
00:33:39.600 --> 00:33:40.460
Client retention?
客户留存率？

792
00:33:40.720 --> 00:33:42.120
You're asking me about client retention?
你在问我客户留存率的事？

793
00:33:42.260 --> 00:33:42.480
Yes.
是的。

794
00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:44.040
Well, I...
嗯，我……

795
00:33:44.040 --> 00:33:50.370
Um, Angela, my sales numbers are not updated,
嗯，安吉拉，我的销售数据没有更新，

796
00:33:50.390 --> 00:33:51.350
so that's on you.
所以那是你的责任。

797
00:33:51.750 --> 00:33:52.910
Stop haranguing me.
